from pathlib import Path
import pandas as pd
import numpy as np
import sys,json
root=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
a=pd.read_csv(root/'results'/'continuous_annual.csv')
e=pd.read_csv(root/'results'/'monthly_episodes.csv')
r=pd.read_csv(root/'results'/'continuous_cost_1x.csv')
base=a[a.cost_multiple==1];double=a[a.cost_multiple==2]
lines=['# Funding carry: initial findings','', 'The first continuous-position feasibility test is positive after the stated cost assumptions in each of 2022–2024. It does not beat the illustrative 5% annual cash hurdle across the full three-year period. This justifies further research, not live deployment or a claim of proven alpha.','', '| Year | Monthly full close/reopen baseline | Continuous hedge, quantity changes only | Continuous hedge, doubled costs |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
m=pd.read_csv(root/'results'/'annual_summary.csv').set_index('year')
for year in [2022,2023,2024]:
 b=base[base.year==year].iloc[0];d=double[double.year==year].iloc[0]
 lines.append(f'| {year} | {m.loc[year,"compounded_capital_return"]:.2%} | {b.return_on_capital:.2%} | {d.return_on_capital:.2%} |')
lines+=['', 'Returns use total account capital, including spot purchase and cash collateral equal to the spot holding’s entry value. They are simulated in USDT, with monthly resizing and no collateral interest. They are not returns on futures margin alone. The continuous account begins with 10,000 USDT, grows to '+f'{r.wealth_end.iloc[-1]:,.2f}'+' USDT, and is fully liquidated at the final endpoint. Three-year growth is '+f'{r.wealth_end.iloc[-1]/10000-1:.2%}'+', versus 15.76% from an illustrative 5% compounded annual cash return. A 5% cash hurdle is a scenario, not an audited historical alternative investment.', '', 'The continuous version trades the change in BTC quantity at each monthly rebalance, instead of crossing both legs in full every month. Positions remain equal and opposite in BTC quantity during each holding period. Rebalance sizing solves `2*S*q + k*abs(q-q_previous) = account equity`, where `k` is the assumed two-leg cost per BTC traded. Account cash can be reassigned between spot and futures at these monthly boundaries. No intramonth collateral transfers are assumed.', '', 'This execution change was investigated after seeing the monthly-close baseline; it is an economically motivated refinement, not an independent out-of-sample success. No entry signal or parameter search was used. The results remain exploratory.', '', 'Data checks: all 3,288 funding payments during the holding windows are present. The audit also checks the initial funding boundary, hence 3,289 expected slots. Native funding calculation timestamps are up to 31 milliseconds after their scheduled boundary; the native timestamps are preserved, and the scheduled slot is used to join the mark-price proxy. Three missing days in monthly mark archives (72 hours) were restored from official daily archives. One intermediate spot-price hour remains absent and is documented; no monthly execution endpoint is missing. No price or funding interpolation was used.', '', 'The hourly-high, 1% maintenance-margin stress proxy reports no breaches. Actual historical maintenance tiers, exchange liquidation procedures, sub-hour paths, operational interruptions, venue default, stablecoin depegging and taxes are not fully modeled. A clean margin proxy does not make this a risk-free trade. Hourly trade-price opens and assumed slippage do not establish executable bid/ask P&L. Funding settlement marks are approximated by mark-price hourly opens.', '', 'Decision: keep intraday options trading paused. Retain unconditional continuous carry as a transparent benchmark. The next research question is whether a forecast of funding persistence can improve returns above both this benchmark and a cash hurdle, without increasing leverage. A profitable historical total alone does not justify adding a signal. See RESEARCH_NOTES.md for the mathematics, fixed rules, assumptions and proposed validation protocol.', '', 'To reproduce: run `python study.py`, `python continuous.py`, `python write_report.py`, then `python -m unittest discover -s . -p "test_*.py" -v` from this folder. Python, numpy and pandas are required. Source data are included; the existing source ZIPs are reused.', '']
(root/'LEGACY_FEASIBILITY.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines))
(root/'results'/'environment.json').write_text(json.dumps(dict(python=sys.version,pandas=pd.__version__,numpy=np.__version__),indent=2))
print('\n'.join(lines[:12]))
